From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 08:43:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent: show a task's output, open its log, and keep the log
 with its record

The tasks card of 0037 said that a background shell was running and for
how long, never what it was printing. The output lived only in the
agent's /tmp/claude-<uid>/.../tasks/<id>.output, on a tmpfs, so a reboot
took it; the Agent Tasks history of 0035 remembered that the task
existed, not what it printed. Story 041.

What it adds, on top of the adapter's _claude/tasks contract version 2
(@lucascouts/claude-agent-acp-plus >= 0.26.0):
- A card row expands (keyboard-reachable "Expand task"/"Collapse task"):
  what the task runs -- its tool call's title, else its description --
  its progress details, and for a shell task the last lines of output in
  a monospace block, or "No output yet". A watched row is expanded;
  every row starts collapsed after a restart.
- "Open Log" on a shell row fetches the output, saves it as the task's
  log and opens it read-only in an editor tab; "Open Thread" on a
  subagent row shows the subagent's own thread when its parent's
  conversation has it loaded, else opens the parent at the tool call
  through 0041's path. A failure reads "Could not open the log: <why>".
- When a shell task ends its output is copied into Zeo's data directory
  and belongs to the history record: the panel's rows offer "Open Log"
  ("Log no longer available" when the file is gone), and Delete, Delete
  All Archived and 0053's Delete Selected delete the log with the row.
  Loading the history sweeps every log no record owns.
- Open Log is refused in a remote project, card and panel alike, with
  task_log::REMOTE_PROJECT_NOTICE ("Open Log is not available in remote
  projects"): a log is a local file, and a remote path would resolve on
  the other host.

Contract (_claude/tasks v2, advertised as agentCapabilities._meta
["_claude/tasks"] = { "version": 2 }; every v1 field and method kept):
- snapshot keys Zeo reads -- required: id, type, description,
  background, depth, status, startedAt; nullable (absent parses as
  None): toolCallId, endedAt, usage, lastTool, summary; defaulted:
  hasOutput (false), tail (none). A tail that is not a list of strings
  keeps the previous task list and logs a warning naming the session.
- _claude/tasks/output { sessionId, taskId, maxBytes: 1048576 } answers
  { content, totalBytes, truncated }. An agent advertising a version
  below 2 gets no request: Zeo answers "unsupported" itself.
- The fixtures claude_tasks_snapshot_v2.json and claude_tasks_output.json
  are byte-identical to the adapter's claude-tasks-snapshot.json and
  claude-tasks-output.json; status.sh step 6 checks both pairs.

File-mode rules (task_log.rs): logs live at <data dir>/agent_task_logs,
scoped by release channel, as <session>/<task>.log, each id mapped to a
separator-free file-name component. The directories are made 0700 and
tightened to it when they already exist; a log file is 0600. A save
writes a temporary file in the log's own directory, sync_all()s it and
renames it over the previous log, so an interrupted save leaves the old
log whole -- never via /tmp, another filesystem. A log keeps at most the
last 1 MiB, cut at a line boundary under "[earlier output truncated: N
bytes]". Log lines (agent_task_log event=saved|deleted|swept|failed)
carry ids, sizes, modes and outcomes, never output text.
The cut searches bytes for that line boundary, so a cap that lands
inside a multibyte character advances to a char boundary, never panics.

Migration: HISTORY_MIGRATIONS step 4 (the next free step; 0053-0055 add
none), ALTER TABLE agent_task_history ADD COLUMN log_bytes INTEGER;
NULL means no log, so a database written before this patch keeps every
record, each without a log. Steps 1-3 are unchanged (append-only).

No new dependency; Cargo.lock is unchanged. Rides claude-agent-acp-plus
BY DEPENDENCY after 0053, the last task patch: it extends 0037's card,
0035's panel and store, 0041's open-at-task path and 0042's delete path.

a4b39c38 review: (2026-11-01, story 072) Checked against upstream
#66255/#66101/#66102. This patch adds no arm to AcpThread::handle_session_update
beyond 0034's, and it does not touch the SessionMessage arm or
subagent_association. The output and log surfaces read the same task entries as
at a5c4ca8b.

Story 064 (2026-11-02): `_claude/tasks` contract version 3 -- an entry may name
the ACP session of the subagent it describes (`childSessionId`), parsed into
AgentTask::child_session_id. It is read as a raw value so a malformed one is
dropped on its own entry with a debug log, never failing the snapshot the way a
wrong-typed `tail` does; absent in versions 1 and 2. It sits beside this
patch's version 2 fields, which is why it is here and not in 0034. 3 tests
(acp_thread_tasks_child_session_tests.rs).
---

