+// Story 041, task 5.2 (store half) — a task's log follows its history record: the size recorded
+// on `TaskLogSaved`, the file deleted with the record, orphans swept when the history loads, and
+// no sweep on the in-memory fallback (R6.1, R6.5, R6.6; Q4). Module path: `store::log`. Wired in
+// `src/store.rs` as
+//
+//     #[cfg(test)]
+//     #[path = "store/log_tests.rs"]
+//     mod log;
+//
+// Every test name starts with `log_` (filter `cargo test -p agent_tasks_panel log_`).
+//
+// Contract (design.md §Task history, §`task_log`): `TasksCardEvent::TaskLogSaved { session_id,
+// task_id, bytes: u64 }`; `HistoryEntry::log_bytes`; `delete_archived` / `delete_all_archived`
+// delete the row, then the file; `finish_loading` sweeps with every loaded key kept, and skips the
+// sweep on the fallback. `agent_ui::task_log::{log_path, write_log}` re-exported for this crate.
+//
+// Contract assumed beyond design.md (the test seam, also used by the card and the panel tests):
+// the log root is read through `agent_ui::task_log::logs_root_in(cx)`, which returns the
+// `agent_ui::task_log::LogsRootOverride(PathBuf)` gpui global when set and `logs_root()` otherwise.
+// Production never sets it; tests set it so nothing touches the operator's data directory. If the
+// implementation picks another seam, change `use_scratch_logs_root` only.
+//
+// Hostile halves first: deleting (s1, t1) must leave (s1, t10)'s and (s2, t1)'s files; a delete
+// whose row write FAILS must delete no file; the sweep must keep every loaded record's file while
+// removing orphans, and must remove NOTHING when the history is the in-memory fallback — an empty
+// fallback history would otherwise delete every log.
+
