+// Story 041, task 6.1 — a card row expands: what the task runs, its progress details, its tail
+// or "No output yet"; watched rows stay expanded; nothing persists; the control is labelled and
+// reachable from the keyboard (R4.1–R4.8; Q16). Filter: `tasks_card::expand`.
+//
+// Wired in `src/tasks_card.rs` beside the other card test modules:
+//
+//     #[cfg(test)]
+//     #[path = "tasks_card/expand_tests.rs"]
+//     mod expand;
+//
+// Contract (design.md §`TasksCard` changes) and what this file assumes beyond it, in the card's
+// existing style:
+//   - `TasksCard::toggle_expanded(session_id, task_id, cx)`; `TaskRow::expanded: bool` (true when
+//     toggled open OR watched) and `TaskRow::running_what: SharedString`;
+//   - `TasksCard::expand_focus_handle(&session_id, &task_id) -> Option<FocusHandle>`, like
+//     `watch_focus_handle`;
+//   - debug selectors `tasks-card-expand-{id}`, `tasks-card-running-what-{id}`,
+//     `tasks-card-tail-{id}`, `tasks-card-no-output-{id}`, and story 013's
+//     `tasks-card-details-{id}`;
+//   - the disclosure's screen-reader label lands in `RENDERED_ARIA_LABELS` like the row's other
+//     controls.
+//
+// Hostile halves first: a task whose tool call is NOT in the thread must not borrow another
+// tool call's title; expanding A's `t1` must not expand B's `t1`; a subagent row expanded shows
+// no tail block and no "No output yet".
